  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Mohd. Umair (As Per Fir Mohd. Umar vs State Of U.P. Thru. Prin. Secy. Home ... on 23 September, 2025 Author: Karunesh Singh Pawar Bench: Karunesh Singh Pawar High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad, Lucknow Bench Neutral Citation No. - 2025:Ahc-Lko:59019 High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad Lucknow Criminal Misc. Anticipatory Bail Application U/S 482 Bnss No. - 1361 of 2025 Mohd. Umair (As Per Fir Mohd. Umar .....Applicant(s) Versus State Of U.P. Thru. Prin. Secy. Home Deptt. Lko And Another .....Opposite Party(s) Counsel for Applicant(s) : Ajey Singh Counsel for Opposite Party(s) Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/55217432/ 1 : G.A. Court No. - 12 Hon'Ble Karunesh Singh Pawar, J. 1.",
    "facts": "The present case has been registered on the basis of an FIR lodged on 14.01.2025 against five persons, including Anas Kirana Store, Khadra. It is alleged that a team of S.T.F. conducted a raid at the house of co-accused Mohd. Arif and recovered adulterated tea leaves. During interrogation, co-accused Arif disclosed that he used to purchase tea from various shops, including Anas Kirana Store owned by co-accused Mohd. Anas @ Mo. Anas. He further stated that the green tea bag, marked with ?Nepal,? had been purchased by him from the present applicant.",
    "arguments": "4. Learned counsel for the applicant submits that the applicant is innocent and has been falsely implicated in the matter. It is contended that the applicant has no connection with the alleged substance. 5. On the other hand, learned AGA, relying upon the case diary, has opposed the bail application. He submits that this is not a case of false implication, as there exists scientific evidence supporting the prosecution case.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "4. Learned counsel for the applicant submits that the applicant is innocent and has been falsely implicated in the matter. It is contended that the applicant has no connection with the alleged substance. 5. On the other hand, learned AGA, relying upon the case diary, has opposed the bail application. He submits that this is not a case of false implication, as there exists scientific evidence supporting the prosecution case.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
